 "tags": {
  "_comment": "TWO DIMENSIONS, BOTH MULTI-VALUED, AND THEY ARE NOT THE SAME QUESTION. `sells` is what a company makes; `buyers` is who buys it. One word carrying both is the defect this file already names under 'a sector is never also a category'. A company can hold several of either.",
  "_derived_comment": "EVERY TAG IS DERIVED, NEVER STORED ON A COMPANY. `sells` comes from vendor_type and `buyers` from the buyer verdict, so there is one writer per fact and no second copy to drift. To change a tag, change the fact underneath it - which is already gated. scripts/tags.py is the only place the derivation lives.",
  "sells": {
   "GovTech Product": "govtech-product",
   "Equipment / Components": "equipment",
   "Engineering / Consulting": "consulting",
   "Services (non-tech)": "services",
   "Distributor / Reseller / Co-op": "distributor",
   "Association / Gov / Media": "association"
  },
  "buyers": {
   "sled": "state, county, city or school district - read off their own pages",
   "federal": "federal agencies. OUT OF SCOPE for this board and unassigned on every record: nothing in this dataset establishes it, and solesourcejobs.com is becoming the federal board.",
   "private": "commercial buyers alongside government. Unassignable today: `names_other_buyers` is null on all 366 answered records, so there is no evidence to read it off."
  }
 }
